# /etc/hjviewer/review.conf: hjv-api's App Review account, the demo login that Apple's App Review
# uses for the iOS app (server/api/README.md, The App Review account; docs/server-runbook.md 7-17).
# Only this file names the account: its ID, its password as a hash, and when it ends. hjv-api uses
# it while HJV_API_REVIEW_FILE names it and UNTIL has not come, and reads it again when it changes:
# no restart. Delete it to end the account (then hjv-api admin user delete tag:<its tag>).
#
# The user writes it in a terminal of their own: python3 -I deploy/review-conf.py --until
# <YYYY-MM-DD> --out ~/review.conf [--pc <demo PC ID>]..., which asks for the ID and the password and
# keeps only the password's hash. Neither the ID nor the password goes into the repository, a chat, a document or a
# commit. The file is root:hjviewer-api 0640, as door 2's. Its lines, each once, and # comments:
#
#   ID=<the login ID; one of HJViewer's ID rule (Z or Y, not ZA) refuses the whole file>
#   HASH=pbkdf2-sha256$<100000 to 10000000 iterations>$<salt, base64 of 16+ bytes>$<key, base64 of 32 bytes>
#   UNTIL=<the UTC time it ends, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ>
#   PC=<1 to 3 different PC IDs, comma-separated: the demo PCs; the one line that may be left out>
#
# The account's access ticket (docs/access-tickets.md 2-4) reaches the PC= IDs only, until UNTIL:
# without the line, the account connects to nothing once hbbs checks tickets. An hjv-api from
# before the access tickets refuses the whole file with the line: put the new hjv-api in first.
#
# Made-up values, as review-conf.py writes them for the password "correct horse battery staple"
# and the date 2026-11-30 (the salt is 00 01 … 0f here; the tool takes 16 random bytes):
#
#   ID=APPREVIEW-TEST
#   HASH=pbkdf2-sha256$600000$AAECAwQFBgcICQoLDA0ODw==$7xdxRO7JQgy8EJPSqLNEqSvFBtDU7JwCjdGfgyTYweY=
#   UNTIL=2026-11-29T15:00:00Z
#   PC=100200300
#
# As it is, this file has none of the lines: there is no App Review account (hjv-api logs "ID,
# HASH or UNTIL is missing").
